<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1609" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăgōn</span></b> ,
		ōnis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγών</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen.</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶνος</span>
			<i>a contest</i> or <i>combat in the
				public games</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gymnicus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 4, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non esse restituendum Viennensibus agona,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 4, 22</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">musicus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 22</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. ib.
			23</span></i>.—Hence, prov.: nunc demum agon est = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῦν γάρ ἐστιν ἀγών</span>, <i>now we must act</i>, <i>now is the time for
				action</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 45</span></i>. </div>
